hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1364","We are told by Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli, we are told by Yazid, meaning Ibn Zurayi, we are told by Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah al-Masoudi, he said: He told me Yazid al-Faqir said that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah being asked about prayer while travelling, which is shorter? He said: No, the two rak'ahs during travel are not shortened, rather shortening one rak'ah when fighting. Then he said: \We were with the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the prayer was established"," and the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," stood up"," and a group stood up behind him"," and another group faced the enemy"," so he led the one behind him in prayer. One rak'ah"," and he prostrated two prostrations with them"," then they set off and took the place of those who were facing the enemy"," and that group came and he led the prayer with them. The Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," performed one rak'ah and prostrated with them two prostrations"," then the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," greeted"," and greeted those behind him. And peace be upon those.” Abu Bakr said: Jabir’s statement: The two rak’ahs during travel are not shortened. He meant they are not shortened from the traveler’s prayer."""
